               z = 0.70-1.00: N =   536, median eta = 2.556, median M500 = 2.19e+14
  canonical  d log eta/dz = +0.1869 +- 0.0129 dex per unit z; the framework requires 0, a LambdaCDM-native rising scale gives about +0.10 dex by z = 0.8 (slope +0.13)
  alt        eta at fixed mass (1e14 - 3e14 Msun), by redshift:
               z = 0.00-0.15: N =   809, median eta = 1.761, median M500 = 1.60e+14
               z = 0.15-0.30: N =  1593, median eta = 1.797, median M500 = 1.72e+14
               z = 0.30-0.45: N =  1306, median eta = 1.889, median M500 = 1.84e+14
               z = 0.45-0.70: N =  1179, median eta = 2.078, median M500 = 2.01e+14
               z = 0.70-1.00: N =   536, median eta = 2.352, median M500 = 2.19e+14
  alt        d log eta/dz = +0.1887 +- 0.0129 dex per unit z; the framework requires 0, a LambdaCDM-native rising scale gives about +0.10 dex by z = 0.8 (slope +0.13)
  [PASS] 68 AGAINST INTEREST -- the cluster residual DOES evolve in eRASS1: eta at fixed mass rises by +0.187 +- 0.013 dex per unit redshift out to z ~ 0.8, where a constant a_0 requires ZERO and even the LambdaCDM-native emergent scale predicts only +0.13.  Fourteen sigma from the framework's requirement, and above the alternative too   (d log eta/dz = +0.1869 +- 0.0129; +14.5 sigma from 0, +4.4 sigma from the LambdaCDM-native +0.13)
  BEFORE this is read as a kill, the two systematics that plausibly produce all of it, stated up front:
    (1) eRASS1's M500 is calibrated on LambdaCDM weak lensing and its X-ray selection at fixed mass changes strongly with z --
        the same trend appears in f_gas(z) at fixed mass, which is a known selection-and-calibration effect, not a measurement;
    (2) the baryon budget uses a fixed stellar prescription with no redshift dependence, and M_gas is the quantity actually measured.
  So the honest verdict is a LIABILITY requiring a selection-controlled sample (X-COP-class, or eRASS1 with a mass-complete cut),
  not a falsification -- but it is on the ledger now, and it points the same way as the MUSE/Ciocan apparent rise at z ~ 1.
  selection caveat, stated: eRASS1's X-ray selection at fixed M500 changes with z, and the M500 proxy is calibrated on
  LambdaCDM weak lensing -- both push on eta(z) at the level measured here.  Quote the bound, not a detection.

